{title: O Little Town of Bethlehem}
{title_ko: 오 베들레헴 작은 골}
{hymnal: 새찬송가 120장}
{artist: Phillips Brooks / Lewis Redner}
{genre: Christmas}
{flow: Meditative}
{style: Carol}
{key: F}
{tempo: 72}
{time: 4/4}
{score: o-little-town-of-bethlehem.abc}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
O [F]little town of [Bb]Bethlehem
How [F]still we see thee [C]lie
A[F]bove thy deep and [Bb]dreamless sleep
The [F]silent stars go [C]by
Yet [Dm]in thy dark streets [Gm]shineth
The [F]everlasting [C]Light
The [F]hopes and fears of [Bb]all the years
Are [F]met in thee to[C]night[F]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
For [F]Christ is born of [Bb]Mary
And [F]gathered all a[C]bove
While [F]mortals sleep, the [Bb]angels keep
Their [F]watch of wondering [C]love
O [Dm]morning stars, to[Gm]gether
Pro[F]claim the holy [C]birth
And [F]praises sing to [Bb]God the King
And [F]peace to men on [C]earth[F]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
How [F]silently, how [Bb]silently
The [F]wondrous gift is [C]given
So [F]God imparts to [Bb]human hearts
The [F]blessings of His [C]heaven
No [Dm]ear may hear His [Gm]coming
But [F]in this world of [C]sin
Where [F]meek souls will re[Bb]ceive Him still
The [F]dear Christ enters [C]in[F]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
O [F]holy Child of [Bb]Bethlehem
De[F]scend to us, we [C]pray
Cast [F]out our sin and [Bb]enter in
Be [F]born in us to[C]day
We [Dm]hear the Christmas [Gm]angels
The [F]great glad tidings [C]tell
O [F]come to us, a[Bb]bide with us
Our [F]Lord Em[C]manu[F]el
{end_of_verse}
